<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Experimental Setup</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Target Models and Testbeds:</span>
We evaluated GPT-20B, LLaMA-13B, and Llemma-7B (Table <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table IV ‣ IV Results ‣ Efficient Fine-Grained GPU Performance Modeling for Distributed Deep Learning of LLM" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV</span></a>) on two distinct HPC platforms: Perlmutter (A100-SXM4) and Vista (H200-96GB HBM3) (Table <a href="#S4.T5" title="Table V ‣ IV-A Experimental Setup ‣ IV Results ‣ Efficient Fine-Grained GPU Performance Modeling for Distributed Deep Learning of LLM" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">V</span></a>). These systems, spanning multi-GPU clusters and unified memory architectures, enable a comprehensive evaluation of our framework’s adaptability across diverse hardware paradigms.</p>
</div>
